{
  "abstract": "This paper replaces the claim that AQFT follows from admissible charts alone. It distinguishes a conditional admissibility-indexed precosheaf from a physical Haag--Kastler net and proves the rigorous bridge currently available: a decomposable coherent projector preserves isotony and spacelike commutation on the compatible subalgebra of an already local upper net. Failure of joint representability does not imply commutation, chart inclusion does not automatically extend observables, and absence of a global chart does not forbid a quasilocal algebra or colimit.",
